// The initializer := gives the initial value of a reference (kbak/clafer-semantics#164).
// A set initializer constrains the set of the instances under the parent, so it stays in the
// context of the parent: [ initially (some xs => xs.dref = 1, 2) ]. The instances created later
// are not initialized.

xs -> integer 0..3 := 1, 2
[ F xs.dref = 3 ]

A 2
    ys -> integer * := 1, 2
    [ F some this.ys ]
